      "content": "okay, i see. so they basically saw partition as a way to avoid a civil war. but looking at it from the perspective of the local leaders, was there a genuine sense that the British were being \"neutral\" or \"fair\" in how they managed those tensions, or was the British role seen more as actively playing the different groups against each other to maintain influence?",
